# Sudoers fragment for stamp-server. Lives at /etc/sudoers.d/stamp-server
# inside the container (root-owned, mode 0440 — required by sudo's own
# file-perm check).
#
# Grants the git user passwordless invocation of stamp-ensure-repo-key
# (and, below, the no-argument stamp-sign-approval helper — AGT-2263),
# and nothing else. These helpers are the only privilege-escalation surface
# the git user has. stamp-ensure-repo-key is hardcoded to:
#   - validate its <owner>/<repo> argument shape strictly
#   - refuse to overwrite an existing key file
#   - chown the resulting file root:git mode 0640
# so even a git-shell escape can only ADD new keys for never-before-
# seen repo specs — it cannot substitute or modify an already-registered
# stamp-mirror deploy key.
#
# The trailing '*' in the command rule lets sudoers admit the helper's
# single positional argument. The helper itself validates the arg; sudoers
# is the access-control gate (who may invoke this binary at all), not the
# input filter.
git ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/local/sbin/stamp-ensure-repo-key *

# AGT-2263: the review-signing private key is root:root 0600 and never
# readable by git. stamp-review (running as git via git-shell-commands)
# signs each approval by piping its canonical bytes to this helper, which
# writes only the base64 signature to stdout. The empty-string argument
# list ("") means sudo admits the command with NO arguments at all. The
# helper itself is the input filter: it signs only a well-formed ApprovalV4
# (exact key set incl. repo_id, strict field shapes, server_key_id equal to
# its own key, issued_at within 5 minutes of now, canonical bytes) — never
# arbitrary bytes — and logs each signature to the container log. env_reset
# (sudo default; no SETENV tag here) keeps the caller from steering the key
# path. See src/lib/approvalSigning.ts.
git ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/local/sbin/stamp-sign-approval ""
